 is a restaurant in Waldemar Thranes gate 8 at St. Hanshaugen in Oslo, Norway. This restaurant appeared in several fictional works including Jo Nesbø's books about Harry Hole and several books by Bjørg Vik."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-restaurant-schr-der"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Restaurant_Schr%C3%B8der"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Norwegian cuisine","links":[["Ekebergrestauranten","dish/ekebergrestauranten"],["Engebret Café","dish/engebret-cafe"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fruktsoppa","dish/fruktsoppa"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Kransekage","dish/kransekage"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Lutefisk","dish/lutefisk"],["Risalamande","dish/risalamande"],["Stortorvets Gjæstgiveri","dish/stortorvets-gj-stgiveri"],["Trollkrem","dish/trollkrem"]]}]},"dish/thali":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/thali","n":"Thali","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 18 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Thali or bhojanam (Telugu: భోజనం bhōjanaṁ, IPA: [bʰoːdʒɐnɐw̃], meaning \"full meal\") is a round platter used to serve food in South Asia, Southeast Asia and the Caribbean. Thali is also used to refer to an Indian-style meal made up of a selection of various dishes which are served on a platter. Thali is also used in South Asia for ceremonial purposes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-thali"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thali"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Afghan cuisine","cuisine/afghan-cuisine"],["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine"],["Bruneian cuisine","cuisine/bruneian-cuisine"],["Burmese cuisine","cuisine/burmese-cuisine"],["Cambodian cuisine","cuisine/cambodian-cuisine"],["Fijian cuisine","cuisine/fijian-cuisine"],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"],["Lao cuisine